  "structure": {
    "block_count": 72,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Want a Good Laugh? Moms Share 17 Hilarious (and Slightly Cringey) Pregnancy Moments",
        "text_sha256": "4e3f7a0b6d82353703cd72d4187f882dd059e758b917c8ccc325291c90484152",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Most embarrassing pregnancy moments",
        "text_sha256": "4602d3f4b185c6a752b55c1b0094549f8acc63192a4f1b57e0ab8ee85947392f",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Pregnancy: oh, the joy, the tears ... and the embarrassment. Here, 17 moms share their most mortifying pregnancy moments.",
        "text_sha256": "1fcb290e3c5b236550a0e2dff5e9310177f7d6a7fd723121c2eb939a78110096",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Pregnancy comes with its fair share of crazy symptoms . Some of them are amazing ( hello, gorgeous hair !). Some of them you will look forward to never having again (sorry, morning sickness). And some of them are, well, just awkward.",
        "text_sha256": "6d81ee2a5a87ceb4fe5f197ca4ac6a085afa8e6ddf1c26ac7d453a230472f02b",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "And that's not to mention all the other (shall we say) cringey pregnancy memories you and your baby bump are bound to make together along the way.",
        "text_sha256": "fdfcaf93001d42f6cbf046f8d43c30e35fd45055edeb3baee2f83719a5a1c1f3",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "These What to Expect Community moms-to-be had the best reactions to the ups and downs that are a normal part of growing a beautiful new baby: They had a good laugh, knowing they’re not alone and it’s only temporary.",
        "text_sha256": "03c1df3b2b47a6bd71b8a1d8f87bfba54ee12f33412a6bcb7a537813525c559b",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Read on as 17 moms share their most hilarious and embarrassing pregnancy moments.",
        "text_sha256": "f73dd227453e06ccd21969e4e09aeae00127cb104132eb07893175ad47d48180",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pregnancy = awkwardness. Yup, embarrassing moments are par for the course when you’re expecting (think farts, tumbles, spills, and more).",
        "text_sha256": "f12c28c912d31c1632d6fbd10515eb3e789e3d40f8e937b1589cdca050e68a61",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Lean into the humor. If you don’t laugh about it, you just might cry, so try to see the funny side of these pregnancy mishaps.",
        "text_sha256": "616b125faa23020df58eb76c67dd7dd5a50a643c76ea8290d8aec7b50f0e6703",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Everyone goes through it. You are definitely not the only pregnant mama who’s had these mortifying moments — share your stories and you’ll feel a whole lot better.",
        "text_sha256": "d01ea7a831d5dda28833f3dde53f84d472c6e94c2bcc313ec6aaeaea7817ab9a",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "1. Can’t a pregnant mama catch a break?",
        "text_sha256": "3557b0cece8a2c463b97e1850e05b512ff8d97a89da9a54ca6c87cb77efb9316",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“After a long week at work, I had to make a trip to Costco. My feet were so swollen and tired that I opted to take one of those electric carts (totally embarrassing). When I was trying to grab a veggie tray, my cart bumped the display and an avalanche of veggies came pouring down all over me. I was mortified!” — purpura1",
        "text_sha256": "0e6d3fe3a6f96a95b72896fb2101fcc9990c058d742b87694c81f934bf7c3fdf",
        "word_count": 63
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "2. Not just another day at the office",
        "text_sha256": "376c5d9afaba66fbc286663dfda7466db83d1c32faa6270985d8216f61d06d44",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I was 30 weeks pregnant at work and thought I was experiencing contractions. My coworkers called the ambulance, and I had to be shuffled to labor and delivery. It turns out I was having pains due to constipation …one of those moments when you put your palm to your face.” — dorkydorkette",
        "text_sha256": "37fe91060cbcc284983557ab6cb29b6324c6261b8470e45a3db3cf5b473fd1f7",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "3. Heads up!",
        "text_sha256": "aa14d7b21f8cf1a9b967781cec860f8da2a86db2ff62885a73d8b797d988c5f8",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I’m a fourth-grade teacher and today when I was walking between the kids’ desks, I totally smacked a boy in the back of the head with my belly.” — ex1tedm0m",
        "text_sha256": "6fad5591d78cd9ab238dc6f6ca417ab08a2a5fabf356e729e2431c9cec4e76bd",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "4. Bumping it forward",
        "text_sha256": "d2ad96d68d4f023fc98fbf3aaf7927054121af1c9f6a0aed83b4d8bfe479ecf7",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I was in an elevator and it got crowded, and the director got on and somehow my bump rubbed her booty (she's really tall and had on heels!). There was an awkward glance, and there has been every time she sees me!” — MrsDRob",
        "text_sha256": "caa7a6f51f9d3a071a27fb95154c7b7b67b73ba9715c5c95571ac33f66e34aef",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Looking for more pregnancy laughs? Download the What to Expect app for a Community of moms who’ve seen it all, plus find expert tips and comforting advice.",
        "text_sha256": "61c410c9a816ee8103b56dd33216b7488ac3cfcc305afa3551bdb044bd038021",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "5. A tight fit",
        "text_sha256": "b34fc2c5e4f5f15b92051d2e4de6cd327eee2a8b6b34e185cc1a56cb146d6a0c",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I squeezed in between my car and another car in a parking lot and got wedged between the mirrors.” — Firsttimemummyaus",
        "text_sha256": "75b37a6439361ea53d9d2396bf2189d1019c0fb0050b70ab7b42138e7251b2db",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "6. Now that’s true love",
        "text_sha256": "fe2502e921f414428957a04b046ef846a19436d6e4c11f51edd31954f87e7b52",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"The other day I said to my husband, 'Is there anything sadder than a pregnant woman putting on pants?' His reply? 'Yeah, honey, there is. I just watched you put on underwear.' I had to laugh!\" — ABD6677",
        "text_sha256": "0c3549517f61807d4ec4490db8c57e63c40185487823c2eb54aefc3f251e9e8d",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "7. It’s nice to meet you, Mrs. Clumsy",
        "text_sha256": "84740e2c44fbf19204535c1e5c98b843012902854331a6bdc4e2b93b25a7e6bd",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I’m 24 weeks pregnant , and my husband and I just moved. We are trying to make new couple friends. Tonight a couple invited us to go on a walk, so we joined them with our dogs. We were standing in a circle talking. I stepped back, rolled my ankle and TOPPLED over!!! I am so clumsy now!” — ellekrand",
        "text_sha256": "e5d910c9f5641590763b991cacb176605348813aa4d282b657eeac8f1437dd5a",
        "word_count": 60
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "What to Expect Community parent bri24det admits to clumsiness too. “I’m constantly spilling things and making more work for myself and bending over or squatting is the last thing I want to do!”",
        "text_sha256": "5b20c91b6684980d7266f67d76deb0205eb153d8fdf8edb3a404b1c6a7f3e912",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "8. Oh, the shame",
        "text_sha256": "d72111a58a3fe02f6d598cd8d20cfb978d09116feef1424686ef1c20655cd2e6",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I farted at work! Ugh, I’m so embarrassed! I thought it’d be silent, but nope. It was like, ‘Blurp, hello world!’ When I realized that other people must have heard it, I had to text my boyfriend, best friends, and sisters. They all laughed, of course, but said to just own it and excuse myself next time. At least I can pull the pregnancy card!” — moonmama2be",
        "text_sha256": "efe55d49e402c17ba69941714fbd72da65e28e41bdc881ebca14d893b87957cb",
        "word_count": 67
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "9. Hormonal holiday",
        "text_sha256": "8bcbce871d2d5ae2973064b3f8d9563f26e1aadef14b584132fdd0930475b271",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I cried when my mom and stepdad got me dishes for Christmas. I was upset because I liked my dishes. I started to bawl my eyes out and sobbed, ‘I am so offended right now!’ I have no idea where it came from…Needless to say, I actually do like the dishes they gave me. I just don’t know why, but it felt like they killed my cat or something.” — B3ccabutt",
        "text_sha256": "940fddcf902d34fd0d8bf4965fcd1244955c4ee20fd24771187a3ea98e1aab95",
        "word_count": 71
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "10. The joy of pregnancy sex",
        "text_sha256": "0749ae42868a75810b23188e0ce25868b8fbbb95fd0e915c1b09a7450d6d856f",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“Mid-act, I accidentally farted. I couldn’t stop laughing. Thankfully my significant other and I are extremely comfortable with each other. We both laid there laughing for a good five minutes. Safe to say, it ruined the moment but made for a good story.” — Firsttimemomma3",
        "text_sha256": "9ef4ce30f6e473bb38d83915668cc77b9ca65aa84c774ee024429f61d1017b55",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "11. Just when you need to rest those feet …",
        "text_sha256": "b1f849ecb43c590002ce200d2f4a8a80485ddabe8205ac929c52161fded26aa4",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I sat down and popped a screw out of the chair. That’s how chairs get murdered.” — betsyws",
        "text_sha256": "aa5a2300d078a0259e54dc86c3dcf7ba25f5643b1774f45904b355f27ea83363",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "12. For better, for worse",
        "text_sha256": "6dae7d920f500f0f18b36fa0e4ad7984d4a533020b7c693189e0ba229b5ddd2f",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“Constipation leads me to very smelly farts. My husband makes fun of me all the time. He opens the windows and asks for help!” — emclean85",
        "text_sha256": "2c0a8b7a7c48853f467aea5a13e1535bc524fe6596cdd38df3596cf0a3b5de86",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "13. Bathroom break",
        "text_sha256": "f1c5adea0fc622b0ccf89fe886686120305da9aed6d59c59056d2f9a5266f1ed",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I broke the toilet seat! I always lean to the left to wipe, which is ridiculously inconvenient because it’s sooooo hard for me to reach, and the toilet seat cracked in half! And I'm not even that heavy!” — May2016Boy",
        "text_sha256": "e618214d614afc7c4f4f7d3d47df6970ec98cf5cd8c9451026c09f2d6f92e674",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "14. Chain reaction",
        "text_sha256": "3ac40b406042ae6d5784515a8bbab05a69befcd5f12ad052c2738271af396ebf",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I was in the middle of a grocery store, and they were handing out samples of egg rolls. I popped one in my mouth and apparently some crumb went down the wrong pipe or something. It sent me into a coughing frenzy and I peed myself — a lot.” — mhaugh2016",
        "text_sha256": "124084fe27104d0eac37084851841fd0a2faf09c9d182d398e2e8eab47d13bee",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "15. Genius move",
        "text_sha256": "935bd03e427340f7d54300fddd407893b2d7435952fec374b68201075b356865",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I was on a four-plus-hour road trip with only my two young boys, a 2- and 1-year-old. I pulled off the highway at a rest stop because I had to go so badly, but they were both sound asleep… So I used one of their diapers to sit on and just peed in my driver’s seat. It was so bittersweet… Yay, pregnancy problems!” — mo3angels",
        "text_sha256": "a7d6543f244b063f55234ab89a6a7cdf0930ba4af7740b37dba0e20e89780289",
        "word_count": 65
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "16. Playful payback",
        "text_sha256": "e5397a330dbc45e931731dc804007c6a27f652e86ec98dd0c95b7ea8e81278e8",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“My husband and I were taking our dog out for a walk, and I started making fun of his outfit. I laughed so hard I peed myself. The worst part was that I was wearing a dress so it came down my legs and I couldn’t stop laughing. It was gross, but hilarious!” — karenlizeht",
        "text_sha256": "279edf7bbc18fcb5e8c6b5a3a9010856bc8575ed725f6bfbd5012c7f3e1fc476",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "17. Let's dance",
        "text_sha256": "393c4faf8300af39ebdfa4175432b9c52faab5081dfbb060a12fbe80e16bd902",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I coughed and peed myself while we were on vacation. I got up off the couch before it went anywhere and my husband was sitting right next to me. I had to pass in front of him to get to my luggage, and he reached up and grabbed my butt. I did a weird dance thing to get away from him, swatted his hand, and yelped. He had no idea what was going on until I told him I had peed myself….Of all the times to get frisky!” — LittleHouseInTheHills",
        "text_sha256": "3eebb49464bb41d178a9cd759c015ed077ce7d9d8dd0c171de8380b61c7a9986",
        "word_count": 90
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This story is meant to reflect individual contributors' experiences and does not necessarily reflect What to Expect's point of view. This content is not intended to be used as medical advice, for diagnosis, or treatment.",
        "text_sha256": "ee0f05c6702eef33001d019d530dd1c6c8b1451571e78998b182e174c2ba2a9a",
        "word_count": 35
